{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC3 — OPERATOR ACTION, not an agent change: the `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` repository secret is absent. Run 31587452003's anthropic arm failed its credential preflight with `::error title=anthropic arm has no credential::Set the ANTHROPIC_API_KEY repository secret`. Adding it requires GitHub repo Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions, which an agent cannot reach — it needs a repository admin.\n\nThe arm's fail-not-skip design is CORRECT and is deliberately unchanged by this ticket's change (Gerrit 1658). The preflight exits non-zero rather than letting the arm skip every llm_live test and report green; the `llm-live-canary` in tests/external/conftest.py is the second, independent defence for the same failure mode (collected>0, executed=0 => exit 1). Do not soften either.\n\nRelated but out of scope, filed separately: the OIDC credential step stays gated to the bedrock arm, so a bedrock-pinned module on the anthropic/openai arms may now fail on AWS *credentials* where it previously failed on region. That is a distinct defect from this ticket's region-resolution signature."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786558251052688001,"uuid":"fedf40a7-9da4-442b-a01d-11ccf92cc2fd"}